{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 92,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A Psalm. A song for the Sabbath day. It is good to praise the LORD, and to sing praises to Your name, O Most High,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "to proclaim Your loving devotion in the morning and Your faithfulness at night",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "with the ten-stringed harp and the melody of the lyre.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For You, O LORD, have made me glad by Your deeds; I sing for joy at the works of Your hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How great are Your works, O LORD, how deep are Your thoughts!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A senseless man does not know, and a fool does not understand,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "that though the wicked sprout like grass, and all evildoers flourish, they will be forever destroyed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But You, O LORD, are exalted forever!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For surely Your enemies, O LORD, surely Your enemies will perish; all evildoers will be scattered.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But You have exalted my horn like that of a wild ox; with fine oil I have been anointed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My eyes see the downfall of my enemies; my ears hear the wailing of my wicked foes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous will flourish like a palm tree, and grow like a cedar in Lebanon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Planted in the house of the LORD, they will flourish in the courts of our God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In old age they will still bear fruit; healthy and green they will remain,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.92.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.92.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "to proclaim, “The LORD is upright; He is my Rock, and in Him there is no unrighteousness.”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
